1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,872
How much does the merchant get today?

2
00:00:01,922 --> 00:00:07,968
At closing time, a shop counts the till, and counting the same day again gives the same answer.

3
00:00:08,018 --> 00:00:11,040
Every night, the bank does that for each website.

4
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:19,416
A business day runs from midnight to midnight in the bank's time zone: the same day that decides reversal or refund, so the two never disagree.

5
00:00:19,466 --> 00:00:23,640
It adds up what was paid, the fee, what was refunded, and the payout.

6
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:28,368
The payout can even be negative, when refunds outweigh the day's sales.

7
00:00:28,418 --> 00:00:34,416
Counting a day again replaces it, never adds to it, so a missed night is simply caught up.

8
00:00:34,466 --> 00:00:40,344
And behind every total is a list of every line, so any number can be explained.

9
00:00:40,394 --> 00:00:43,416
Next: when a buyer says, I never bought this.
